Figure 1: Modality shortcuts and Perturbot . Top: familiar visual, lexical, and
motor cues can replace task evidence (solid: hypothetical shortcut choices;
dashed: required alternatives). Bottom: task-preserving wrist-view
perturbations (V), behavior-supported caption enrichment (C), and screened,
relabeled trajectory segments (R; Section 3.2 ). Examples are conceptual;
relabeled local behavior does not by itself establish recovery.
